# TDD worktree base-SHA marker (per-worktree, never commit)
.tdd-base-sha
.tdd-issue
# The TDD working files, generated from the versioned templates next to them.
# Ignored rather than merely "do not commit this": the phase agents stage with
# `git add -A`, so a rule nobody can enforce is a rule that gets broken — the
# spec reached a feature branch that way once, and only a history rewrite got it
# out. An ignored file cannot be swept in at all.
tdd/feature.md
tdd/REVIEW.md
# The knowledge graph, in full. Every file under it is regenerated by
# `graphify update .` (AST-only, no API cost) and nothing in the build, the tests
# or CI reads any of it — the only reference left in the repository was the line
# in tdd/cleanup.sh that committed them.
#
# The two big blobs went first (3.6 MB per regeneration, a 63k-line diff for a
# directory rename, which no pull request can honestly carry). The rest followed
# for worse reasons:
#
#   - .graphify_python holds an absolute path into one machine's uv toolchain,
#     so it is wrong for every other clone and rewritten on the next update;
#   - cost.json is a local ledger of token counts per run;
#   - GRAPH_REPORT.md was kept because "its diff is readable", but cleanup.sh
#     regenerates it *after* the merge, in its own commit on develop — so that
#     diff never reaches a reviewer and the justification did not hold.
graphify-out/
